# scripts/verify-deploy-smoke.sh copies a sandbox CA here to inject into a verification
# build, and deletes it on exit — but not if it is killed outright. A certificate is not
# a secret, yet a stray one in the repository is exactly the generated-file-that-looks-
# like-source problem that nearly committed a transient tsconfig once already.
.verify-ca.crt
